Z||000000||FieroSoul||07-13-2001||07:47 PM||||  My 84 coupe has an GT style steering wheel in it.  Don't know if how it got there (original?).  Anyway the Fl sun is melting whatever is inside. Sometimes this brown play do like stuff seeps out the seams. The leather seems to be stretching too.<BR> Anyone ever take one of these apart and rebuild it.  Doesn't seem too hard just cut the threads, redo the inside and sew it back up.  Maybe bondo would work to replace this play do crap.  Anyone with any experience or just plain good ideas??||||reg||8
Z||000001||Fleabitdog||07-13-2001||09:40 PM||||Fierosoul, Welcome to the forum. I have taken them apart but have not tried to repair them yet. I don't beleive it would be ver hard if the leather is still good. Dave<p>[This message has been edited by Fleabitdog (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSoul||07-13-2001||10:03 PM||||Thanks for the welcome. I think the leather is okay.  Just got to decide what to put inside after I get rid of the play do?? Another idea might hard black foam insulation.  What do you think?||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||07-13-2001||10:05 PM||||If it were me I would be looking for another steering wheel, either from the wreckers or aftermarket.  Cause those steering wheels take a lot of abuse with no power steering.<P>my thoughts anyway..||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||07-14-2001||12:19 AM||||Not sure about what to do about the steering wheel, but if your car is an SE it probably came with a 3-spoke wheel but it is not the same as the later GT wheels. It is not as thick as the GT wheels and also the leather doesn't go as far down the spokes. At least that is what my 84 SE came with... I know there are companies that redo wheels but I have no idea how.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ed||07-14-2001||12:54 AM||||I made a fix on mine by just putting a drop of household cement (glue) over the stitches where the leaks were.  That was several years ago. The fix worked.  <P>I am going to replace the wheel now because the underlying padding is just giving up.  I have a new wheel, and am about to put it on.  <P>The Fiero Store has replacement wheels.<P>P.S.  I asked the forum before about the simplicity of replacing the wheel.  The response was universal that it was very simple.  No one mentioned the turn indicator cancelling tower.  Does that pose a problem? How about the riveted (?) plate attached to the metal of the wheel.  Nobody mentioned that either.  Does THAT pose a problem?  <P>P.P.S  I see now the other thread about steering wheels.  And rivets!  None of the shop manuals mentioned no stinking rivets!  So what's the real story about replacing an '87 GT's steering wheel?  Rivets, center nuts, wheel pullers, et al?   <P>[This message has been edited by Ed (edited 07-14-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Ed (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fformula88||07-14-2001||10:42 AM||||I have replaced my wheel with the Fierostore wheel, and can try to explain it all if needed.  Enyone who needs some advice go to the other thread active "damn fierostore steering wheel".  There is also the link to my original thread on the topic from a few months back.  Also email me if there are anymore ?'s.<P>Ed, I am trying to answer your ?'s in the other thread||||reg||1
